  "findings": [
    "SheetBlock1.initMap aligns each Sea, translates minY to cumulative height, then advances by that Sea height. Sea.doAlign uses atom dimensions and starting altitude. emit_message_label's current-minus-previous ascent increment is algebraically consistent with this baseline transition, with no fitted constant.",
    "Twelve fresh valid four-stripe alternating-size, forward/reverse/self/reverse-self/external and inline bold/italic/underline controls match after. Two heading-form controls remain whole failures: Java paints Crest/Ridge, while Rust paints literal '= Crest'/'== Ridge' and measures different text/canvas. This is present before and after and remains a consumer/creole limitation, not a new regression.",
    "Rust notes and dividers do not call emit_message_label: Event::Note owns line_top plus line_metrics.ascent / EnhancedNoteBody; Event::Divider directly calls text_render::emit_text. Their two control sources remain whole failures in both revisions and are explicitly outside the changed message emitter. No transfer of the new baseline formula is claimed.",
    "present_bold_empty and style_parameter_contrast are both whole failures in before and after exact CLI replay. This checkout has no concurrent shared style/creole/text_render/WBS production, and these findings certify no combined behavior."
  ],
